KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
This test passed only vacuously until the parameter-pack-arity fix: the tuple
elements are compile-time constants, so std::get<0> of t == 1 was folded to
true and the assertion removed before symbolic execution -- std::get was never
exercised at run time.

Resolving a directly-deduced type-internal parameter pack to its full arity
during the deferred method-body drain -- the fix this accompanies -- makes
std::get<0> a genuine run-time call.  The run-time std::get chain
std::get -> std::__get_helper -> std::_Tuple_impl::_M_head ->
std::_Head_base::_M_head is not fully instantiated, so the call returns a
nondet value and the assertion no longer holds: VERIFICATION FAILED.

This is a known bug in the run-time std::get chain instantiation, a separate
layer from the pack-arity fix.  Flip back to CORE once that chain instantiates
correctly so the assertion is verified non-vacuously.
